      "before": "a1-u03-d07-e01",
      "title": { "en": "The third gender: neuter" },
      "body": { "en": "Nouns that end in -o or -e are usually neuter: dziecko, pytanie. With them \"my\" is moje and \"your\" is twoje. So: mój brat, moja siostra, moje dziecko." }
    },
    {
      "id": "a1-u03-d07-t02",
      "before": "a1-u03-d07-e10",
      "title": { "en": "Dzieci and rodzeństwo" },
      "body": { "en": "Dzieci is \"children\", the plural of dziecko (\"my children\" is moje dzieci). Rodzeństwo is one word for brothers and sisters together. Masz rodzeństwo? Tak, mam." }
    }
  ],
